<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Soyo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Soyo was a coastal province of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-kongo">Kingdom of Kongo</a> at the mouth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congo-river">Congo River</a>. It was where the Portuguese first made contact with Kongo in the 1480s. Accounts of the Kongo Empire list it among the core provinces under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manikongo">manikongo</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/soyo.jpg" alt="Soyo" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Edward Middleton · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Casper_on_the_move.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
